# component: collapsible
# decisions: DOC-1, DOC-2, MOT-14
# hunks:
#   MOT-14 (operator, 2026-11-13, agent chat ground up): `CollapsibleContent` animates its height
#     and opacity both ways on Base UI's `--collapsible-panel-height` and its starting/ending style
#     attributes, the idiom upstream's own Accordion uses: `duration-state` + `ease-enter` in,
#     `duration-state-exit` + `ease-exit` out, `overflow-hidden` so the content is clipped while it
#     grows. Upstream's panel is unstyled, so every fold snapped. The caller's `className` lands on
#     an inner `collapsible-content-body` wrapper, the shape upstream's Accordion uses, so padding,
#     gap and flex layout the caller adds sit INSIDE the animated box: a padded panel collapses to
#     zero rather than to its padding, and a `hiddenUntilFound` panel leaves no blank band while
#     closed; the panel itself takes `w-full min-w-0` (it fills its row even in an `items-start`
#     column, and never forces it wider), since a caller's `w-full min-w-0` now sits one level in. Reduced motion collapses both transitions through base.css (MOT-5), so nothing here
#     restates it.
#   DOC-2: the `cn` import from `@vegastack/design`, needed now that the panel merges a className.
#   DOC-1: prettier's reflow plus the provenance header the three-copy model needs.
